# Baseline does NOT read secrets from the repository.
#
# All configuration lives in your private runtime folder, outside OneDrive and outside Git:
#   Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%\Baseline\config.env
#   (override the folder with the BASELINE_HOME environment variable)
#
# Create / edit it with hidden prompts (nothing ends up in shell history):
#   npm run configure            # app password + Google OAuth client
#   npm run configure -- status  # what is set (never prints values)
#
# Keys used in config.env (or as real environment variables on a server, which take precedence):
#   APP_PASSWORD_HASH     scrypt hash of your app password      (set by `npm run configure`)
#   SESSION_SECRET        random, generated                     (set by `npm run configure -- init`)
#   ENCRYPTION_KEY        random 32 bytes, encrypts tokens      (generated — back it up in a password manager)
#   APP_BASE_URL          http://localhost:3000 (later your Tailscale HTTPS URL)
#   HOME_TIME_ZONE        IANA zone, e.g. Europe/Brussels
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID      Google OAuth web client
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET  Google OAuth web client secret
#   BACKFILL_DAYS         initial history import, default 365
#   DATABASE_PATH         optional; default %LOCALAPPDATA%\Baseline\data\baseline.db (must be outside OneDrive/repo)
#
# The Hevy API key is entered in the app (Settings) and stored encrypted in the database.
#
# Development only (non-secret, may be set in the shell):
#   DEMO_MODE=1           fictional demo data from ./data/demo.db (refused in production)
